  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 139 PM CDT Sat Aug 29 2026\n\nShowers/Storm Trends...Area of light to moderate rain continues \nto trek across the region this afternoon as a mid-level shortwave/\ntrough and weak surface warm front move through. This area will\nshift to the east by around sunset, with additional more isolated\nto scattered shower activity expected later this evening into\nSunday morning as another frontal boundary lifts northward and\nweak WAA/moisture advection occurs. Lack of instability has not \nallowed for any thunder today. Slightly better chance for some \nthunder tonight as elevated CAPE spreads in from the south/west, \nso will continue with a slight chance of thunder. PWATs do climb \nto around 2 inches overnight, but any heavier rain looks to be \nvery isolated with chances of over an half inch of rain under 50%.\n\nOn Sunday into Tuesday, most of the period is looking dry, but as\ninstability builds in the warm sector with a surplus of moisture \nand instability, especially on Monday (MUCAPE of 2000-3000 J/kg),\nalong with the stationary boundary in the region and possible \nweak shortwaves crossing the region, storms will be possible at\ntimes. But a weak cap will help keep a lid of storm activity. Not\nsurprisingly, CAMs and other models are all over the place with \nlocation/timing of storm chances. AI/ML highlighting much of the \narea for an increased threat for severe storms somewhere in this \ntimeframe, but pinning down when will be challenging. So a lot of \nif's, but if anything can form, it could be on the strong or \nsevere side with gusty winds and hail possible, along with \ntorrential downpours. Will need to monitor these features and\ntrends over the next few forecast runs to better assess the \nsevere weather threat.\n\nTemps & Humidity Levels...The clouds and rain kept high temps \nbelow normal today, mainly in the 60s to low 70s. As the warm \nfront lifts north, temps will climb above normal on Sunday into \nthe upper 70s to mid 80s, and even warmer on Monday and Tuesday \nwith highs in the mid to upper 80s with a few spots topping out \naround 90. The south flow will usher in humid conditions on \nSunday and Monday as well, with dew points increasing into the \nupper 60s and low 70s. Depending on cloud cover and precip \nchances, heat indices on Monday may rise into the low to mid 90s.",
